#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""resident: the resident iOS session (user 2026-11-11). The phone stays booted in iOS; every stream thread submits jobs to it; one owner holds
the phone lock for the session. Rules: AGENTS hard rule 3 / docs/RULES.md H3 (parks in fastboot when idle > 30 min, low or falling battery, crash,
session end). Recipe: super repo docs/recipes/resident-session.md. Decisions: tools/resident_core.py (pure, host-tested by tools/test_resident.py).

Submit (any thread; never touches the phone itself):
  resident submit --stream gpu|bt|wlan|tools --est S [--max S] [--prio 1..9] [--profile NAME|any] [--label L]
                  [--push SRC:DST]... [--restart NAME]... [--run "/abs/prog args"]... [--hot "hot subcommand args"]... [--wait-for REGEX]...
                  [--sleep S]... [--pull SRC:HOSTDST]... [--host "cmd {dir}"]...          steps run in the order given (--host after the log cut)
                  [--expect REGEX]... [--expect-absent REGEX]...                           oracles on the job's own USB-log slice + step output
                  [--kernel K] [--args "k=v ..."] [--overlay TREE]                         a KERNEL job: batched into ONE reboot at the next boundary
                  [--thread ID | --notify none] [--follow] [--no-start] [--dry-run]
      Prints `JOB id=<id> ...`. Files are copied at submit time (a later edit does not change the job). Without a running session one is started
      (`phone-lock run --owner resident --detach`, it waits for the current holder through the lock). At the end the thread gets ONE line
      `RESIDENT JOB END id=.. stream=.. result=PASS|FAIL|CUT|CRASH|NOTRUN dir=<slice dir> why=..` (phone-lock's notify, t3 thread send). CRASH = the session
      crashed while this job ran (panic, stall, watchdog reset, xrun gone); every other waiting job then ends NOTRUN and the phone parks.
  resident follow ID [--timeout S]        block until job ID has a result; prints it (exit 0 PASS, 1 otherwise, 3 timeout)
  resident status                          session, boot, battery, queue
  resident cancel ID                       a queued job ends NOTRUN; a running one is cut at its next check (CUT, GAP line)
  resident start [--kernel K] [--floor MV] [--max S] [--set key=value]...   start a session now (normally submit does it);
                                          --floor/--set: THIS session only; lasting settings: config.json "settings"
  resident reserve --stream S --from HH:MM --to HH:MM | --clear    a window (UTC today) where only stream S's jobs start; before it, other
                                          streams' jobs start only if their --max ends before it opens (demo slots)
  resident owner [--stream KEY --thread ID]   the thread that gets KEY's job notices (handoff: the old one becomes 'former');
                                          submit --owner KEY (or $PIXOS_OWNER) routes a job's notices to KEY's current owner
  resident end [--reason TEXT] [--now]    graceful: finish the running job, then end (the phone parks). --now = phone-lock end (job cut)
  resident _serve                         the session owner (run by start under phone-lock run; not for hand use)
Files: $RESIDENT_DIR (default ~/pixelios-artifacts/resident): config.json (kernel, settings), profiles.json (boot profiles; example
tools/resident-profiles.example.json), queue/, jobs/<id>/ (job.json, files/, steps.log, result.json), session.json, events.log.
Every refusal, cut or skipped job is a `RESIDENT GAP:` line in events.log, the job's steps.log and its result (rule 7).
Last line of every command: RESULT: PASS|FAIL|ERROR resident ...
"""
